# L §6.4 from D: "A move the scenario declares books nothing before D: an instance whose day, or a window's first day,
# falls before D is left out". extra is dated window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10), which starts before from 2027-01-01:
# left out by its window's first day, whatever day it takes (writer 8: no windows clause is needed; windows earliest
# and latest are gone). So konto keeps its opening, 100.00 PLN, in early as in the base. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED
# §6.4, a scenario move booking before from through a window day; tally 2.2 (2.2-6) drops late_, whose leg stated
# its own day.)
# tally 2.2.1 (S-from, L §6.4 as the round rules it: "an instance whose day falls before D is left out"): a window across
# D is decided by L §4.4: extra books on the window's days from D on, so e is the hole naming xday.
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

version base
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask b: bal(konto, 2027-12-31)
=== early.tally
scenario early over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

input xday: date
input xamt: money PLN

move extra: transfers
  on xday
  leg cash from konto to world amount xamt

version ex
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-06-01
  xday = window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) "plan"
  xamt = 10.00 PLN "plan"

ask e: bal(konto, 2027-12-31) in early
=== expect
b: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
e: ?"date within window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) not precise enough for a balance" (extra)
  unknown day: xday
  world: early
  cut 2026-10-20
